course: dictionary
lesson: 3697
title: Fish that lie flat
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A flatfish is a fish with a flat body. It lies on one side on the sea floor. The word tells you the shape: flat, and a fish. Context helps you check this. Read the words around flatfish and look for clues about where it lives and how it moves.
explain: «The mimic octopus copies the shape and movement of dangerous animals like sea snakes and flatfish.» The sentence says the octopus copies flatfish, so flatfish must be animals with a shape and movement that are easy to notice. Try your meaning in the sentence: a flat fish that lies on the sea floor fits well.
explain: Plaice, sole, flounder, halibut and turbot are all flatfish. Fish and chips can be made with plaice, so you may have eaten a flatfish without knowing it. When you meet a new word, check the other words in the sentence before you look it up.
fact: A flatfish has a flat body and lies on one side on the sea floor.
fact: As a flatfish grows, both of its eyes end up on the upper side of its head.
fact: Plaice, sole, flounder, halibut and turbot are all flatfish.
fact: «Flatfish» is a noun. It can be singular or plural: one flatfish, or two flatfish or flatfishes.
fact: The mimic octopus, discovered in 1998 off Indonesia, copies the shape and movement of flatfish and other dangerous animals.
exercise: «The mimic octopus copies the shape of flatfish.» What is a flatfish? | A kind of seaweed that grows on rocks | *A fish with a flat body that lies on one side on the sea floor | A bird that flies low over the sea | A large animal that lives in the sea and breathes air
exercise: Which of these is a flatfish? | Shark | Dolphin | *Plaice | Crab
exercise: In a flatfish, where do both eyes end up as it grows? | Inside its mouth | *On the upper side of its head | On the underside of its body | On its tail
test: Name one flatfish. | Trout | Herring | *Turbot | Salmon
test: Where was the mimic octopus discovered? | Brazil | Australia | Scotland | *Indonesia
exam: «The mimic octopus copies the shape and movement of flatfish.» What does copies mean? | Hides from | Swims past | Eats | *Makes a close imitation of
